course: dictionary
lesson: 2707
title: A medicine from a plant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some plants are poisonous, yet people can still use them to make medicine. Digitalis is a medicine made from the foxglove plant.
explain: Read the context: «Foxgloves are poisonous, but the medicine digitalis made from them has helped heart patients since the doctor William Withering wrote about it in 1785.» The word but shows a contrast: the plant is dangerous, but the medicine helps people.
explain: Digitalis is a noun for a medicine, so think of it as a thing you can take, not a thing you can eat. When you meet a word like this, ask what job it does in the sentence, then check your meaning fits.
fact: Digitalis is a medicine made from the foxglove plant.
fact: The foxglove is a tall plant with purple or white bell-shaped flowers.
fact: Doctors use digitalis to help a weak heart beat more strongly and steadily.
fact: Foxgloves are poisonous, so never eat any part of the plant.
fact: Medicine is only safe in the right dose, given by a doctor.
exercise: What is digitalis? | A kind of grass used to feed sheep | A sweet fruit that grows on tall bushes | *A medicine made from the foxglove plant | A bird that lives near water
exercise: In «Foxgloves are poisonous, but the medicine digitalis made from them has helped heart patients», find and copy one word that means harmful to eat. | *poisonous | heart | patients | medicine
exercise: Why should you never eat a foxglove, even though digitalis helps people? | Because it makes you grow taller | Because it tastes very sweet and sticky | *Because it is poisonous and medicine is only safe in the right dose | Because it is a type of grass
test: What do doctors use digitalis to help? | *To make a weak heart beat more strongly and steadily | To make a cold go away in one day | To make bones grow longer | To stop the sun from shining
test: Which description fits the foxglove plant? | A type of cheese made from milk | A round, hard stone found in rivers | *A tall plant with purple or white bell-shaped flowers | A small bird with a long, thin beak
exam: Which statement about digitalis is true? | It is a sweet fruit, so you can eat as much as you like | It can be picked from any garden and taken without a doctor | *It is a medicine made from foxgloves, and it is only safe in the right dose given by a doctor | It is a poison that doctors never use
